SUMMARY:Fjord
LOCATION:West Newton Cinema\, 1296 Washington St\, Newton\, MA 02465
DESCRIPTION:Times: 3:30pm\, 7pm\nMihai and Lisbet Gheorghiu\, a Romanian-No
 rwegian Pentecostal couple\, move with their five children from Romania to
  Norway after Mihai’s parents die\, seeking closeness to Lisbet’s fami
 ly\, who share their faith. Settling in an isolated coastal village\, they
  form a bond with their neighbors\, the Halbergs. When their daughter Elia
  appears at school with bruises\, suspicions arise about the family's stri
 ct religious upbringing. Fjord explores clashing worldviews\, conformity\,
  tolerance\, and the boundaries of freedom and intimacy.\nhttps://www.west
 newtoncinema.com/movie/fjord\nFrom Pushpin Boston: https://pushpin.city/bo
 ston/
URL:https://www.westnewtoncinema.com/movie/fjord
